# 9. DEDUPLICATION ENGINE

This is a critical feature.

The same business may appear in several sources with different spellings, addresses, or phone formats.

Implement automatic deduplication while preserving all useful information.

Use multiple matching signals:

- Normalized phone number.
- Business name similarity.
- Arabic name similarity.
- French name similarity.
- Address similarity.
- Geographic proximity.
- Website domain.
- Social media URLs.
- OpenStreetMap identifiers.
- Other stable source identifiers.

Use appropriate methods such as:
- Unicode normalization.
- Arabic text normalization.
- French accent normalization.
- Transliteration.
- Fuzzy string matching.
- Geographic distance calculations.
- Weighted matching scores.

### Matching decisions

High-confidence duplicates:
- Automatically merge.
- Preserve all unique fields.
- Preserve all original source records.
- Preserve source URLs.
- Preserve collection dates.
- Record the merge history.

Uncertain duplicates:
- Send to the manual review panel.

Clearly different businesses:
- Keep separate.

Important rules:

Two branches of the same company must not automatically become one business.

A shared phone number alone must not be sufficient evidence for merging.

Do not delete original source evidence.

Maintain a complete merge history and allow the user to reverse an incorrect merge.

